<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman conquest of Egypt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1517">1517</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Selim I's conquest of Egypt · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-mamluk-war-1516-1517">Ottoman–Mamluk War (1516–1517)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> was the campaign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selim-i">Selim I</a> that ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> rule in 1517. Following victory at Marj Dabiq in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 1516, Ottoman forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. The conquest ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> and the shadow Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> maintained in Cairo, the last institutional remnant of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-conquest-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Ottoman conquest of Egypt" width="281" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Asherbooks.com · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Ottoman-Mamluk_war_and_the_conquest_of_Mecca_and_Medina._Printed_in_Basel,_dated_1518.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
